# The counters are a cost (CR 602.2b), paid when the ability is activated, so the Drake is made even if Hatcher is gone
# when it resolves: the ability on the stack is independent of its source (CR 113.7a). Hatcher hits for 1 on turns 3, 5 and
# 7 (no spell is cast, so no prowess), making three counters. On turn 7 it removes them for the Drake, and Bot2 answers by
# burning the 1/3 Hatcher with Lightning Bolt. Hatcher dies; the Drake still arrives.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Drake Hatcher
Island x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Drake Hatcher.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Drake Hatcher)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Drake Hatcher)
[T7 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Drake Hatcher)
[T7 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Drake Hatcher.Counters.Incubation = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Drake Hatcher.Activate(Ability: Create a 2/2)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Drake Hatcher)
Bot2.Pass
[T7 Bot1.End]

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Drake Hatcher
Bot1.Battlefield = Drake Token; Island; Mox Sapphire
